# @ p_anic< "message" stops the program with error[panic] at the call;
# it type-checks wherever it stands (here an Int result and a Char).
== SOURCE
u:s_ize := { k -> k > 3 ? @ p_anic< "bad grid size {k}"; k * 2 }
u:s_ize 2
c := "ok" c_at @ p_anic< "never here"
u:s_ize 5
== ERROR
error[panic]: never here at 90..112
